     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>In base 14:</p>\n<p>A represents the digit 10.</p>\n<p>B represents the digit 11.</p>\n<p>C represents the digit 12.</p>\n<p>D represents the digit 13.</p>\n<p>You can use the base 14 multiplication table created in an earlier exercise.</p>\n<p>Use the multiplication table for base 14. Find 32 in the product part of the table where 4 is the column header. The answer is the row header, B, for that cell.</p>\n<p>The answer is B<sub>14</sub>.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "B<sub>14</sub>"
    }
   ],
